  "title": "Sack of Mainz",
  "summary": "On 28 October 1462 troops of Adolf II of Nassau conquered and plundered Mainz, the climax of the Mainz Diocesan Feud that began after Pope Pius II removed Archbishop Diether of Isenburg in 1461. The city lost its liberties that day. One source adds that Fust's printing office was set on fire and Gutenberg suffered losses.",
